sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant CLI
    participant Agent as Agentic Loop
    participant LLM as LLM (Groq)
    participant Gate as Confirmation Gate
    participant MCP as MCP Client
    participant RAG as docs-rag server
    participant FS as Filesystem server
    participant Shell as run_command (local)

    Note over User,Shell: Confirm mode. Task: "Make GET /books/{id} return 404 for missing books, add a test, run the tests."
    User->>CLI: types the task
    CLI->>Agent: run(task)
    Agent->>Agent: fit context to token budget
    Agent->>LLM: messages + 13 tool schemas (stream)
    LLM-->>Agent: tool call: docs-rag__search_docs("return 404 not found error")
    Agent->>CLI: on_tool_start (cyan panel)
    Agent->>Gate: search_docs risky?
    Gate-->>Agent: no (read-only), run it
    Agent->>MCP: call_tool(docs-rag, search_docs)
    MCP->>RAG: tools/call
    RAG->>RAG: embed query, ChromaDB top 20,<br/>cross-encoder rerank + rank fusion, keep 4
    RAG-->>MCP: 4 passages from tutorial/handling-errors.md (HTTPException)
    MCP-->>Agent: result
    Agent->>CLI: on_tool_end ✓ preview
    Agent->>LLM: + tool result
    LLM-->>Agent: tool call: filesystem__read_text_file("app.py")
    Agent->>MCP: call_tool(filesystem, read_text_file)
    MCP->>FS: tools/call
    FS-->>Agent: app.py contents
    Agent->>LLM: + tool result
    LLM-->>Agent: tool call: filesystem__edit_file(app.py, raise HTTPException(404))
    Agent->>CLI: on_tool_start (yellow panel, shows the edit)
    Agent->>Gate: edit_file risky?
    Gate->>CLI: ask permission
    CLI-->>User: Allow this action? [y/N]
    alt user types y
        User->>CLI: y
        CLI-->>Gate: approved
        Gate-->>Agent: approved
        Agent->>MCP: call_tool(filesystem, edit_file)
        MCP->>FS: tools/call
        FS-->>Agent: git-style diff of the change
    else user types n
        User->>CLI: n
        Gate-->>Agent: declined
        Agent->>LLM: "The user declined this action..."
    end
    Agent->>LLM: + tool result
    LLM-->>Agent: tool call: run_command("python -m pytest -q")
    Agent->>Gate: run_command risky?
    Gate->>CLI: ask permission
    User->>CLI: y
    Agent->>Shell: run pytest in the workspace (timeout 120 s)
    Shell-->>Agent: exit code 0, "3 passed"
    Agent->>LLM: + tool result
    LLM-->>Agent: final answer (no tool calls), streamed
    Agent->>CLI: on_token ...
    CLI-->>User: "corvus › GET /books/{id} now returns 404 ... all 3 tests pass."
